@startuml

start

:Power management subsystem governed by priority-based RTOS scheduler;
:Continuously monitor voltage rails and battery state via PMIC and BMS;

if (Remaining power < 20%?) then (yes)
  :High-priority task initiates low-power mode entry sequence;
  fork
  :Check charging status;
  if (Connected to supply?) then (no)
    :Reduce CPU frequency;
    :Disable non-essential peripherals;
    :Execute power-saving strategy;
  else (yes)
  end if

  fork again
    :Background task with lower priority;
    :Monitor for change in charging state;

  if (Charging not detected within defined period?) then (yes)
    :Escalate to deep power-saving mode;
  else (no)
  end if
 end fork
else (no)
end if

:Periodic telemetry monitor task driven by timer interrupts;
:Sample system data;
:Employ digital debouncing for events;
:Log to ring buffer protected by mutex;
:Implement fault recovery routine using staged exponential backoff;
:Use CRC-verified commands;
:Ensure bounded retries;

stop

